Z||000000||MooCow||03-29-2000||03:09 PM||||I just went and looked at a Fiero today and the owner is selling it for a grand.  It is all red and the paint is slightly faded but not bad.  The interior is very mint condition looking.  It is an se 4cylinder with a 4 speed manual tranny. It has 96,000 on it.  Did not get a chance to see if it stated cause the owner was not there.  <BR>What year is this fiero?? <BR>Is it an 85 se?<BR>Also if I were to get it could I put on a 86 se nose and dropp in a 3.4 or 3.8 into this Fiero????????????<BR>thanks for all the replies         Ken||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||03-29-2000||03:17 PM||||If it's a 4cyl with a 4spd it's probably an 84. 1984 was the only year for a 4spd with a 4cyl. 85 and up had a 5spd.||||reg||1
Z||000002||ChadMan||03-29-2000||04:37 PM||||That's definitely an 84, unless someone took the time and effort to swap a 4-speed into a later-model car and I can't see that happening.  Look at the rear deck lid - if there's a black grille in the middle (no "humped" deck lid), it's an 84.<P>$1000 is a fair price for a good-running, never-wrecked 84, even with the paint starting to fade.  But 84s are notorious for electrical problems.  If it doesn't run well (hesitation, stumbling, etc.), walk away unless you want to spend a lot of time and money troubleshooting the electrical system.||||reg||1
Z||000003||BAM-BAM||03-29-2000||11:37 PM||||  MooCow,<BR>  Hey Moo, look on E-Bay, there is an 85GT, black, all power options in great condition.<BR> One problem it has a bad valve, and the engine is torn apart. The guy lives in your neck of the woods and is desperate. Right now the high bid is $460.00 and has been for a couple of days. He will send pics if you want. I would snatch it up in a heartbeat if I did'nt live so far away. It would be a great learning experience(working with the motor)and the price is right. I would'nt pay more than $600.00 though. You have a big advantage with the V6 over the Four. The four(stock) doesn't do the Fiero justice. The way I see it, $600.00 and some head work, and your off. That might be a little optomistic but not to far from right on. Give it a look.<P><BR> Thanx, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <BR>||||reg||6
